    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>Although the 6845 provides cursor blinking, the CGA produces its own
blink timings for the cursor and  for blinking text, by ticking this 4-bit 
counter.

It is synchronized via ~RESET&apos; so that normally it is in sync with the 
6845&apos;s blinking.  The net effect is unnoticeable in normal operation
except for the fact that you cannot disable blinking via the 6845.

This logic does not, however, account for the 6845&apos;s &quot;slow blink&quot; mode,
and if set the cursor will blink at the combination of both blink signals.

The text ~BLINK signal ends up half the rate of ~CURSOR_BLINK.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="2660" y="-740"/>
    </visualElement>
