    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>These two chips are where the primary color generation happens.

The MUX_A and MUX_B inputs form two bits that select four of 16 inputs that create the RGBI pixel.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="1720" y="-1160"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>mux_table.dig</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>Label</string>
          <string>MUX Table</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="2560" y="-1040"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Rectangle</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>RectHeight</string>
          <int>42</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectInside</string>
          <boolean>true</boolean>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Label</string>
          <string>U22 &amp; U23: MUX Control</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectWidth</string>
          <int>43</int>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="7020" y="-780"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Tunnel</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>rotation</string>
          <rotation rotation="2"/>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>NetName</string>
          <string>RA</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-440" y="600"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>12</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>The Character ROM holds fonts for both the MDA and CGA cards. 
The CGA has two fonts, one of which is a &quot;thin&quot; font that cannot be accessed without
bridging pads on the card to pull A11 low.

Normally, A11 and A12 are high, which selects the last quarter of the ROM where the
normal CGA font resides.

The address is constructed of the first three bits of the CRTC&apos;s row scan counter, with
the character code value making up the other 8.  This will produce a byte of data 
representing a single scanline slice of a character glyph.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-520" y="380"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U33</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>snapToGrid</string>
          <boolean>false</boolean>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-220" y="590"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>12</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>The CC latch latches the first byte of a video memory read cycle.
In text mode, this is the  character code.
In graphics mode, this is the first byte of pixel data, but it is still referred to
as the &apos;CC&apos; or character code byte.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="40" y="360"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>12</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>The AT latch latches the first byte of a video memory read cycle.
In text mode, this is the attribute byte.
In graphics mode, this is the second byte byte of pixel data, but it is still referred
to as the &apos;AT&apos; or attribute byte.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="540" y="360"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Rectangle</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>RectHeight</string>
          <int>45</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectInside</string>
          <boolean>true</boolean>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Label</string>
          <string>U7 &amp; U8: Color Serializers</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectWidth</string>
          <int>46</int>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="760" y="-840"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>These two chips serialize out pixel data for medium-resolution graphics mode.

Their outputs are C0 and C1 which represent a pair of bits that make up a 2bpp pixel.
C0 is the even bit, and C1 is the odd bit.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="780" y="-800"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>A high STR or &quot;Strobe&quot; input forces all the outputs of the multiplexers low, generating black.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="1720" y="-800"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Rectangle</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>RectHeight</string>
          <int>39</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectInside</string>
          <boolean>true</boolean>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Label</string>
          <string>U38: 6845 Cathode Ray Tube Controller</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectWidth</string>
          <int>54</int>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="1020" y="320"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>The Color Control (CC) register provides various color signals.
The complete 4 bits of the overscan/background color is defined here.
The intensity and blue bits of the &apos;palette&apos; are also selected.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="2140" y="360"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>The 6845 CRTC is a somewhat complex LSI device and a full analysis of its operation is a bit out of scope.
The 6845 here is implemented in Verilog - it is a simple implementation without many of the 6845&apos;s tricker edge cases.
For the definitive description of the 6845&apos;s operation, see Logon System&apos;s &quot;CRTC Compendium&quot;</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="1040" y="1020"/>
    </visualElement>
