    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>Signals with ~OVERBARS indicate that this signal is active-low, ie, 
it is logically true when the logic level is 0.

Therefore GRPH may indicate &quot;in graphics mode&quot; and ~GRPH 
&quot;not in graphics mode&quot;

A trailing tick &apos; on a signal means that this signal eventually 
generates the final undecorated signal after additional logic or 
delays.

Small triangles are tunnels - these make &quot;wireless&quot; connections 
to all other tunnels of the same name. This just simplifies the diagram.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="2300" y="3120"/>
    </visualElement>
