      <pos x="4600" y="-780"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>16</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This 7404 Hex Inverter produces the complement of several control signals.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="4620" y="-740"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>16</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>These chips perform two main functions. Firstly, they produce the MUX_A and MUX_B signals. 

MUX_A and MUX_B are inputs to the color multiplexer and  determine the color source used for rasterization.
(See U9 &amp; U10)

U22 also produces the ~SEL_BLUE signal which is used by the color multiplexers to control the blue channel.

U23B is also used as an OR gate unrelated to MUX logic, which is not shown here.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="7040" y="-740"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U15A</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>snapToGrid</string>
          <boolean>false</boolean>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="6525" y="-248"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U13A</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>snapToGrid</string>
          <boolean>false</boolean>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="6649" y="-288"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Rectangle</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>RectHeight</string>
          <int>42</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectInside</string>
          <boolean>true</boolean>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Label</string>
          <string>U20 &amp; U21: Miscellaneous Signal Logic</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>RectWidth</string>
          <int>49</int>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="5860" y="-780"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>14</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>This pair of chips, a hex inverter (U20) and a D-type flip-flop (U21) perform minor signal logic.

U20 directly produces the ~RESET&apos;, ~DEN, and SEL_BLUE signals from their complements.

HS,VS enter the flip flop directly, while CURSOR and DEN pass through both the inverter and the flip flop.

The flilp flop is clocked via HCLK and produces complementary signals that are delayed, and thus have the &apos;DLY&apos; suffix.

~HSYNC_DLY and ~VSYNC_DLY are delayed by one HCLK.
~CURSOR and ~DEN are fed back into the flip flop, and thus are delayed by two HCLKs. 

Additional logic stages follow, shown here as simplified gates for simplicity of wiring:

• The ~CLR_SR signal is derived from ~DEN, ~DEN_DLY, and VIDEO_EN.  This clears the shift registers when not in the active display area.

• The ~BLANK signal is derived from NOR of HSYNC_DLY and VSYNC_DLY as either hsync or vsync is considered the &quot;blanking period&quot;</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="5880" y="-740"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U65B</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>snapToGrid</string>
          <boolean>false</boolean>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="4103" y="3650"/>
    </visualElement>
    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U3D</string>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>snapToGrid</string>
          <boolean>false</boolean>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="-1384" y="-188"/>
    </visualElement>
