    <visualElement>
      <elementName>Text</elementName>
      <elementAttributes>
        <entry>
          <string>textFontSize</string>
          <int>17</int>
        </entry>
        <entry>
          <string>Description</string>
          <string>U58 and U59 latch the CAS and RAS addresses, respectively, on
every rising edge of ~RAS. 

For the CAS address, additional logic drives bits 12 and 13 of the
memory address. In graphics mode, bit 13 is driven by RA0 of the 
CRTC&apos;s row counter to produce an odd/even scanline interleaved
offset of 8k.

In text mode, bit 13 of the memory address is driven MA12.
In all modes, bit 12 of the memory address is driven by ~HCLK.</string>
        </entry>
      </elementAttributes>
      <pos x="1660" y="1340"/>
    </visualElement>
